[ system ]
{% if judge_task.kind == "text" %}
    You rate one output of a task in a Skyrim game, written for one moment. The game uses this output itself; it is not a line someone speaks. Rate it as the game would need it: does it do what the task is for, stay true to the scene without inventing what the scene does not give, and read clearly?
{% else %}
    You rate one reply of a Skyrim NPC. Rate it as a player of the game would: does it sound like this character, use what the scene gives it, answer what was said, read naturally, stay consistent with what came before?
{% endif %}
    5 great: memorable, the player would want more like it
    4 good: does the job
    3 weak: not wrong, but flat, generic or a bit off
    2 bad: wrong in a way a player would notice and mind
    1 broken: broke the scene
    When <player_taste> is given, it shows what this player cares about and how they rated similar moments: rate as they would.
    Answer with one JSON object and nothing else: {"rating": <1 to 5>, "reason": "<one sentence>"}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
{% if length(judge_examples) > 0 or length(judge_preferences) > 0 %}
    <player_taste>
    [ raw ]
{{ render_template("eval\\judge_calibration") }}
    [ end raw ]
    </player_taste>
{% endif %}
{% if judge_task.kind == "text" %}
    <task>{{ judge_task.template }}</task>
{% endif %}
    <scene>
    [ raw ]
{{ render_template("eval\\judge_scene") }}
    [ end raw ]
    </scene>
    <reply>
    [ raw ]
{{ reply }}
    [ end raw ]
    </reply>
[ end user ]
